            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Portuguese for the landslide, then the Portuguese for to bury under earth or rubble."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: a ambulância",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "a ambulância — \"the ambulance\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A ambulância chegou em dez minutos. The ambulance arrived in ten minutes."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Chamar uma ambulância — to call an ambulance."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ambulância came from French ambulance (EtymDB), first a field hospital that moved with an army, built on ambulant \"walking\", from Latin ambulāre \"to walk\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
